            "contribution_type": "sourcing",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Look for underlying issues.  Some kids, like some adults, are simply naturally slender and have trouble putting on weight.  However, you should try to rule out other reasons for your child's difficulty in gaining weight.<ref>https://www.nationwidechildrens.org/family-resources-education/700childrens/2014/03/why-isnt-your-baby-gaining-weight-and-when-should-you-worry</ref>[[Image:Increase Weight in Children Step 1 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Consult your child’s physician.  If your child is receiving regular medical check-ups, the pediatrician may be the one who informs you that your child would benefit from increasing his or her weight.  But never be afraid to raise the subject if you are concerned.<ref>https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/failure-thrive.html</ref>[[Image:Increase Weight in Children Step 2 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*If peanut allergies are an issue, almond butter can be a good alternative.  Flaxseeds and flaxseed oil also provide ample calories and nutrients."
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Look for underlying issues.  Some kids, like some adults, are simply naturally slender and have trouble putting on weight.  However, you should try to rule out other reasons for your child's difficulty in gaining weight.<ref>http://pubs.ext.vt.edu/348/348-271/348-271.html</ref>[[Image:Increase Weight in Children Step 1 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Consult your child’s physician.  If your child is receiving regular medical check-ups, the pediatrician may be the one who informs you that your child would benefit from increasing his or her weight.  But never be afraid to raise the subject if you are concerned.<ref>http://www.nhs.uk/Livewell/Goodfood/Pages/Underweightyoungchild.aspx</ref>[[Image:Increase Weight in Children Step 2 Version 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*If peanut allergies are an issue, almond butter can be a good alternative.  Flaxseeds and flaxseed oil also provide ample calories and nutrients.<ref>http://www.washingtonpost.com/blogs/on-parenting/post/underweight-child-heres-how-to-put-on-a-few-healthy-pounds/2012/09/24/42a5ecdc-0691-11e2-a10c-fa5a255a9258_blog.html</ref>"
                ]
            }
